'''Calvar'ion''' is a weaker variant of [[Vet'ion]] who is fought in the [[Skeletal Tomb]], a [[singles-plus combat]] area in level 21 [[Wilderness]]. To enter Calvar'ion's lair, players must have completed the [[Wilderness Diary#Hard|hard Wilderness diary]], '''OR''' they must have a Vet'ion boss Slayer task (a skeleton Slayer task does not bypass the diary requirement).

Compared to Vet'ion, the fight is quicker and safer at the cost of an overall lower loot value. 

Killing Calvar'ion counts as a [[Vet'ion]] alternative for a slayer Boss task, the [[Wilderness Diary#Elite|elite Wilderness diary]] task, and the combat achievements.

Upon any player entering the tomb, all players inside will be unable to [[teleport]] for 3 [[ticks]]. This delay no longer occurs after completion of the [[Wilderness Diary#Hard|hard Wilderness diary]].

== Fight overview ==
{{Main|Calvar'ion/Strategies}}Calvar'ion is resistant to any combat style other than [[crush]], and as he is [[undead]], he is susceptible to the [[Salve amulet]] and its [[Salve amulet (e)|enhanced]] version.

Calvar'ion primarily attacks with targeted magic, launching lightning strikes that damage in a 3x3 radius around the arena upon attacking. While he appears to swing his sword during these animations, they do not deal any melee damage, and [[protection prayers]] are ineffective against the lightning. Indirect hits will deal less damage than a direct hit. Occasionally, he may prepare for a shield bash if players are near him, indicated by shadows targeting an area in front of him. Players caught in the targeted area, (or standing underneath him), when he bashes his shield will take damage and be rendered unable to attack for a few seconds.

Calvar'ion is fought similarly to the [[Kalphite Queen]] in that he has two forms, a "normal" and "enraged" form. When he reaches half health in his first form for the first time, he summons two level 115 [[Skeleton Hellhound (Calvar'ion)|skeleton hellhounds]] that attack with powerful melee, and must be killed as they grant him complete damage immunity while alive. Upon being forced into his next stage, Calvar'ion will become enraged and unleash a blast of energy around him, working the same as the targeted magic attack. In this form, he will attack faster (5t attack speed), his attacks will deal more damage, and any drained Defence levels will be restored. Upon reaching half health in this form, he summons two level 139 [[Greater Skeleton Hellhound (Calvar'ion)|greater skeleton hellhounds]] that are even stronger (although still sharing the same health) and must also be killed.

Like the Kalphite Queen, if players don't kill his second form within 5 minutes, he'll revert to his normal state.{{bug|Calvar'ion occasionally spawns only 1 or 0 skeletal hellhounds.}}

